§ `Section 2 -- what a society is`

#ASSERT `the group is a society` `a ten-person book club`
#ASSERT `the group is a society` `a sixty-person hiking club`

-- "10 or more": nine is not a society, ten is.
#ASSERT NOT `the group is a society` `a nine-person book club`

-- Each exclusion.
#ASSERT NOT `the group is a society` `a fifty-person registered company`
#ASSERT NOT `the group is a society` `a statutory association of forty constituted by an Act`
#ASSERT NOT `the group is a society` `a twelve-person limited liability partnership`
#ASSERT NOT `the group is a society` `a registered trade union`
#ASSERT NOT `the group is a society` `a registered platform work association`
#ASSERT NOT `the group is a society` `a registered cooperative society`
#ASSERT NOT `the group is a society` `a registered mutual benefit organisation`
#ASSERT NOT `the group is a society` `an association of foreign insurers under a foreign insurer scheme`
#ASSERT NOT `the group is a society` `a school management committee`

-- The business exclusion in paragraph (g): sole purpose of gain AND not more than 20 persons.
#ASSERT `the group falls within the business exclusion in paragraph (g)` `a twelve-person partnership formed solely for gain`
#ASSERT NOT `the group is a society` `a twelve-person partnership formed solely for gain`
#ASSERT NOT `the group is a society` `a twenty-person partnership formed solely for gain`

-- Twenty-one tips it over: a profit-making partnership of 21 that is not a registered company is a society.
#ASSERT NOT `the group falls within the business exclusion in paragraph (g)` `a twenty-one-person partnership formed solely for gain`
#ASSERT `the group is a society` `a twenty-one-person partnership formed solely for gain`

-- "Sole" purpose: a group formed for gain AND something else is a society.
#ASSERT `the group is a society` `a twelve-person group formed for gain and for something else too`

#ASSERT NOT `the group is a society` `fifty people who are not a club, company, partnership or association`

-- s 2 "officer".
#ASSERT `the person is an officer of the society` `the president`
#ASSERT `the person is an officer of the society` `the secretary`
#ASSERT `the person is an officer of the society` `a member of the committee`
#ASSERT `the person is an officer of the society` `a person holding a position analogous to one of those`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is an officer of the society` `the treasurer who is not on the committee`
#ASSERT NOT `the person is an officer of the society` `an ordinary member`

§ `The Schedule -- specified societies`

#ASSERT NOT `the society is a specified society` `an ordinary hiking club`
#ASSERT `the society is a specified society` `a society representing a religion`
#ASSERT `the society is a specified society` `a political party`
#ASSERT `the society is a specified society` `a society called the National Chess Club`
#ASSERT `the society is a specified society` `a society called the Singapore Chess Club`

-- Item 3's exception covers "Singapore" used as a place of registration, and nothing else.
#ASSERT NOT `the society is a specified society` `a society called the Chess Club of Singapore, where Singapore only shows where it is registered`
#ASSERT `the society is a specified society` `a society called the National Chess Club of Singapore, with Singapore showing the place of registration`

#ASSERT `the society is a specified society` `a society for animal rights`
#ASSERT `the society is a specified society` `a society discussing the governance of the Singapore society`
#ASSERT `the society is a specified society` `a society promoting a language`

-- "Whether primary or otherwise": an incidental activity is enough.
#ASSERT `the society is a specified society` `a hiking club that sometimes discusses a language policy`

#ASSERT `the society is a specified society` `a society formed under the instruction of a foreign government`
#ASSERT `the society is a specified society` `a society mainly funded from outside Singapore`
#ASSERT NOT `the society is a specified society` `the Rotary Club, mainly funded from outside Singapore`
#ASSERT `the society is a specified society` `alumni of a foreign university`
#ASSERT `the society is a specified society` `a society with an office bearer from a society dissolved under section 24 two years ago`
#ASSERT `the society is a specified society` `a society with an office bearer convicted of unlawful expenditure of a society's funds`
#ASSERT `the society is a specified society` `a society with an office bearer the Minister has declared unfit`
#ASSERT `the society is a specified society` `a martial arts school`
#ASSERT `the society is a specified society` `a society organising a lottery`
#ASSERT `the society is a specified society` `a society that exists to promote an offence`

-- THE GAP IN ITEM 10(c). The Schedule refers to a person "declared in writing by the Minister" to be unfit. The
-- Act gives the Registrar that power in s 12(1)(b) and gives the Minister none.
#ASSERT `section 12(1)(b) empowers the Registrar to declare a person unfit to act as an officer`
#ASSERT NOT `any section of the Act empowers the Minister to declare a person unfit to act as an officer`

§ `Fixtures -- section 4 and 4A`

GIVEN `rules insufficient` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `unlawful or prejudicial` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `application non-compliant` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `national security` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `political not citizens only` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `political foreign connection` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `branch of a dissolved society` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `dispute among members` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `name objectionable` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `directed provisions missing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Section4Facts
DECIDE `a section 4 application` `rules insufficient` `unlawful or prejudicial` `application non-compliant` `national security` `political not citizens only` `political foreign connection` `branch of a dissolved society` `dispute among members` `name objectionable` `directed provisions missing` IS
    Section4Facts WITH
        `the Registrar is satisfied the rules are insufficient for proper management and control` IS `rules insufficient`
        `the Registrar is satisfied it is likely to be used for unlawful purposes or purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order` IS `unlawful or prejudicial`
        `the application does not comply with the Act or the regulations` IS `application non-compliant`
        `the Registrar is satisfied registration would be contrary to national security or interest` IS `national security`
        `it is a political association whose rules do not confine membership to citizens` IS `political not citizens only`
        `it is a political association with a foreign connection the Registrar considers contrary to national security or interest` IS `political foreign connection`
        `it is a branch of, or connected with, a dissolved or previously refused society` IS `branch of a dissolved society`
        `a dispute exists among members as to officers or property` IS `dispute among members`
        `the name is misleading, deceptively similar, identical to another's, or undesirable in the Registrar's opinion` IS `name objectionable`
        `the rules lack provisions the Registrar has directed` IS `directed provisions missing`

#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar must refuse a specified society` (`a section 4 application` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may refuse a specified society` (`a section 4 application` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- The six mandatory grounds in s 4(2).
#ASSERT `the Registrar must refuse a specified society` (`a section 4 application` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Registrar must refuse a specified society` (`a section 4 application` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Registrar must refuse a specified society` (`a section 4 application` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Registrar must refuse a specified society` (`a section 4 application` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Registrar must refuse a specified society` (`a section 4 application` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Registrar must refuse a specified society` (`a section 4 application` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE)

-- The discretionary grounds in s 4(3) and (3A) permit refusal and do not require it.
#ASSERT `the Registrar may refuse a specified society` (`a section 4 application` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar must refuse a specified society` (`a section 4 application` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Registrar may refuse a specified society` (`a section 4 application` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Registrar may refuse a specified society` (`a section 4 application` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar must refuse a specified society` (`a section 4 application` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Registrar may refuse a specified society` (`a section 4 application` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar must refuse a specified society` (`a section 4 application` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)

GIVEN `unlawful or prejudicial` IS A BOOLEAN, `national security` IS A BOOLEAN, `rules insufficient` IS A BOOLEAN, `name undesirable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Section4AFacts
DECIDE `a section 4A application` `unlawful or prejudicial` `national security` `rules insufficient` `name undesirable` IS
    Section4AFacts WITH
        `the Registrar is satisfied it is likely to be used for unlawful purposes or purposes prejudicial to public peace, welfare or good order` IS `unlawful or prejudicial`
        `the Registrar is satisfied registration would be contrary to national security or interest` IS `national security`
        `the rules are insufficient for proper management and control` IS `rules insufficient`
        `the name is undesirable in the Registrar's opinion` IS `name undesirable`

#ASSERT `the Registrar must refuse a society that is not specified` (`a section 4A application` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the Registrar must refuse a society that is not specified` (`a section 4A application` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)

-- Insufficient rules and an undesirable name are mandatory grounds under s 4 and are not mandatory under s 4A.
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar must refuse a society that is not specified` (`a section 4A application` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar must refuse a society that is not specified` (`a section 4A application` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `a mandatory refusal ground in section 4 is absent from section 4A` (`a section 4A application` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `a mandatory refusal ground in section 4 is absent from section 4A` (`a section 4A application` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `a mandatory refusal ground in section 4 is absent from section 4A` (`a section 4A application` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE)

-- "May register" with no stated grounds: the discretion is not confined to the mandatory list.
#ASSERT NOT `section 4A confines the Registrar's discretion to refuse to the stated grounds`

#ASSERT `the Registrar may treat a section 4A society as registered under section 4` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may treat a section 4A society as registered under section 4` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar may treat a section 4A society as registered under section 4` FALSE TRUE

§ `Appeals to the Minister`

#ASSERT `the Act provides an appeal to the Minister` `a refusal to register a specified society under section 4`
#ASSERT `the Act provides an appeal to the Minister` `a refusal to register a society under section 4A`
#ASSERT `the Act provides an appeal to the Minister` `a refusal to approve a branch under section 9`
#ASSERT `the Act provides an appeal to the Minister` `a refusal to approve a change of name or rules under section 11`
#ASSERT `the Act provides an appeal to the Minister` `a refusal to consent to the use of a flag, symbol or insignia under section 13`

-- Thirty days for four of them.
#ASSERT `the number of days allowed for the appeal` `a refusal to register a specified society under section 4` EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `the number of days allowed for the appeal` `a refusal to register a society under section 4A` EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `the number of days allowed for the appeal` `a refusal to approve a branch under section 9` EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `the number of days allowed for the appeal` `a refusal to approve a change of name or rules under section 11` EQUALS JUST 30
#ASSERT `an appeal is in time` `a refusal to register a specified society under section 4` 30
#ASSERT NOT `an appeal is in time` `a refusal to register a specified society under section 4` 31

-- s 13(2) states no period at all.
#ASSERT `the number of days allowed for the appeal` `a refusal to consent to the use of a flag, symbol or insignia under section 13` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `an appeal is in time` `a refusal to consent to the use of a flag, symbol or insignia under section 13` 400

-- No appeal is provided against these four.
#ASSERT NOT `the Act provides an appeal to the Minister` `an order to furnish information under section 10`
#ASSERT NOT `the Act provides an appeal to the Minister` `an order to change name or rules under section 11A`
#ASSERT NOT `the Act provides an appeal to the Minister` `a declaration that a person is unfit to be an officer under section 12(1)(b)`
#ASSERT NOT `the Act provides an appeal to the Minister` `an order of dissolution under section 24`
#ASSERT NOT `an appeal is in time` `an order of dissolution under section 24` 1

§ `Sections 6 and 7 -- ceasing to exist, and dissolving`

GIVEN `notification published` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `copy sent` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `months elapsed` IS A NUMBER,
      `proof furnished` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `Registrar satisfied` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `second notification published` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `in fact still active` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A CessationFacts
DECIDE `a cessation` `notification published` `copy sent` `months elapsed` `proof furnished` `Registrar satisfied` `second notification published` `in fact still active` IS
    CessationFacts WITH
        `the Registrar published a notification calling for proof of existence` IS `notification published`
        `a copy was sent to the registered address or by email` IS `copy sent`
        `months since the notification` IS `months elapsed`
        `the society furnished proof of its existence within 3 months` IS `proof furnished`
        `the Registrar is satisfied the society has ceased to exist` IS `Registrar satisfied`
        `a second notification was published in the Gazette` IS `second notification published`
        `the society is in fact still active` IS `in fact still active`

#ASSERT `the society is deemed to have ceased to exist` (`a cessation` TRUE TRUE 3 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

-- THE DEEMING DOES NOT DEPEND ON THE SOCIETY HAVING ACTUALLY CEASED, nor on the copy having been sent.
#ASSERT `the society is deemed to have ceased to exist` (`a cessation` TRUE TRUE 3 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `the society is deemed to have ceased to exist` (`a cessation` TRUE FALSE 3 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the deeming depends on the society having actually ceased` (`a cessation` TRUE TRUE 3 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `a failure to send the copy under section 6(1A) prevents the deeming` (`a cessation` TRUE FALSE 3 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

-- It needs the three months, the Registrar's satisfaction, and the second publication.
#ASSERT NOT `the society is deemed to have ceased to exist` (`a cessation` TRUE TRUE 2 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the society is deemed to have ceased to exist` (`a cessation` TRUE TRUE 3 FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the society is deemed to have ceased to exist` (`a cessation` TRUE TRUE 3 FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `the society is deemed to have ceased to exist` (`a cessation` FALSE TRUE 5 FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE)

GIVEN `informed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `president signed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `secretary signed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `treasurer signed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days taken` IS A NUMBER,
      `Registrar satisfied it was in accordance with the rules` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A VoluntaryDissolution
DECIDE `a voluntary dissolution` `informed` `president signed` `secretary signed` `treasurer signed` `days taken` `Registrar satisfied it was in accordance with the rules` IS
    VoluntaryDissolution WITH
        `the Registrar was informed in writing of the proposal` IS `informed`
        `the president signed the certificate` IS `president signed`
        `the secretary signed the certificate` IS `secretary signed`
        `the treasurer signed the certificate` IS `treasurer signed`
        `days between the dissolution and sending the certificate` IS `days taken`
        `the Registrar is satisfied it was dissolved in accordance with its rules` IS `Registrar satisfied it was in accordance with the rules`

#ASSERT `the certificate meets section 7(1)` (`a voluntary dissolution` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 7 TRUE)
#ASSERT `the Registrar must publish the notification under section 7(2)` (`a voluntary dissolution` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 7 TRUE)

-- One week is seven days; eight is late. All three officers must sign.
#ASSERT NOT `the certificate meets section 7(1)` (`a voluntary dissolution` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 8 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the certificate meets section 7(1)` (`a voluntary dissolution` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE 3 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the certificate meets section 7(1)` (`a voluntary dissolution` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE 3 TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `the certificate meets section 7(1)` (`a voluntary dissolution` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE 3 TRUE)

-- The Registrar's satisfaction is separate: a perfect certificate for a dissolution contrary to the rules gets no notification.
#ASSERT NOT `the Registrar must publish the notification under section 7(2)` (`a voluntary dissolution` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE 3 FALSE)

